          "prompt": "Choose the meaning of this sentence.",
          "label": "Understand the pattern",
          "display": {
            "text": "为了让大家都能来，我需要再想一下。",
            "pinyin": "wèile ràng dàjiā dōu néng lái ， wǒ xūyào zài xiǎng yīxià 。",
            "meaning": "To make it possible for everyone to come, I need to think again.",
            "audio": "18dde420011c557235988dce41bcb03b080a71ecc2e9e8ccf7e8056c1c9eacea"
          },
          "resultDomain": "Grammar comprehension",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "BANK-G-hsk3-purpose-EX-GRAM-G-hsk3-purpose-facet-1-meaning-c1",
              "label": "I need not think again because making it possible for everyone to come does not matter.",
              "labelLanguage": "en",
              "correct": false,
              "feedback": "To make it possible for everyone to come, I need to think again. 为了 introduces the intended purpose of the following action. It explains what someone hopes to achieve, not proof that the goal has already been achieved. Verb + 了…就… can compress an ordered plan: complete the first action and then do the next. Unlike 为了, it need not state a purpose explicitly."
            },
            {
              "id": "BANK-G-hsk3-purpose-EX-GRAM-G-hsk3-purpose-facet-1-meaning-c2",
              "label": "To make it possible for everyone to come, I need to think again.",
