              "feedback": "为了 introduces the intended purpose of the following action. It explains what someone hopes to achieve, not proof that the goal has already been achieved. Verb + 了…就… can compress an ordered plan: complete the first action and then do the next. Unlike 为了, it need not state a purpose explicitly."
            }
